# dayz must be a regular user (UID 1000 or higher), not a system user: journald keeps a journal of
# its own only for regular users, and `dzo logs` (journalctl --user) reads that one. A system user's
# service logs end up in the system journal, which it may not read. sysusers picks a free UID from
# the top of the range, away from the accounts adduser creates from 1000 upwards. An existing
# dayz user is left as it is.
r - 1000-59999
u dayz - "DayZ server operator" /var/lib/dzo -
